export default {"id":"launchkey-level-4","number":4,"title":"The 61 Key Keybed Performance Characteristics","skillBand":"Textbook","duration":"From the course textbook","summary":"The 61-note semi-weighted waterfall keybed is the primary pitch input surface of the Launchkey MK4 61. This module details the default pitch spans, Middle C reference standards, octave transposition mechanics, semitone transposition offsets","modules":[{"id":"launchkey-m-4-1-1","code":"4.1","title":"The 61-Key Keybed Performance Characteristics","blurb":"The 61-note semi-weighted waterfall keybed is the primary pitch input surface of the Launchkey MK4 61. This module details the default pitch spans, Middle C reference standards, octave transposition mechanics, semitone transposition offsets","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"launchkey-l-o-11","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Section 4.1 — Range, Octave Shifting & Pitch Transposition","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Module Overview","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"The 61-note semi-weighted waterfall keybed is the primary pitch input surface of the Launchkey MK4 61. This module details the default pitch spans, Middle C reference standards, octave transposition mechanics, semitone transposition offsets, dual-button reset shortcuts, and the mathematical boundaries of MIDI note generation."},{"type":"heading","text":"Learning Objectives","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["State the default power-on pitch range of the 61-key keybed and define the Middle C reference note.","Execute octave transpositions across the full <code>-3</code> to <code>+3</code> range and interpret LED brightness telemetry.","Perform the simultaneous dual-button octave reset shortcut.","Execute semitone transpositions across the <code>±12</code> semitone range and perform the Shift-assisted transpose reset.","Formulate the behavior of the internal MIDI engine when transpositions push physical keys beyond standard MIDI note limits (0–127)."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"launchkey-l-4-1-1","title":"4.1.1: Default Power-On Keybed Span","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"4.1.1: Default Power-On Keybed Span","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Upon initial power-on, the 61 physical keys are mapped to a 5-octave span:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                  DEFAULT KEYBED PITCH ASSIGNMENT                        |\n+-------------------+-----------------------------------------------------+\n| Keybed Boundary   | Musical Note Name  | MIDI Note Number (Hex / Dec)   |\n+-------------------+--------------------+--------------------------------+\n| Lowest Key (Far Left)  | **C1**        | Note 36 (0x24)                 |\n| Middle Reference Key   | **C3** (Middle C)| Note 60 (0x3C)              |\n| Highest Key (Far Right)| **C6**        | Note 96 (0x60)                 |\n+-------------------+--------------------+--------------------------------+</pre>"},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Nomenclature Standard</em>: In Novation's architecture, <strong>C3 is Middle C</strong> (MIDI Note 60, 261.63 Hz)."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"launchkey-l-4-1-2","title":"4.1.2: Octave Shifting Range & Visual Telemetry","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"4.1.2: Octave Shifting Range & Visual Telemetry","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"The <code>Octave -</code> and <code>Octave +</code> buttons shift the keyboard span in discrete 12-semitone (1-octave) increments:"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Transposition Span</strong>: Maximum <strong>+3 octaves</strong> (Span: C4–C9) down to <strong>-3 octaves</strong> (Span: C-2–C3).","<strong>LED Brightness Feedback</strong>:","<em>No Shift (0)</em>: Both buttons unlit or baseline dim.","<em>Shift Offset ±1</em>: Active button illuminates dimly.","<em>Shift Offset ±2</em>: Active button illuminates with medium intensity.","<em>Shift Offset ±3</em>: Active button illuminates at maximum (100%) brightness.","<strong>OLED Readout</strong>: Displays the shift value and resulting note span (e.g., <code>Octave: +1 (C2-C7)</code>)."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"launchkey-l-4-1-3","title":"4.1.3: Instantaneous Dual-Button Octave Reset","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"4.1.3: Instantaneous Dual-Button Octave Reset","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"To instantly return to the default C1–C6 range during live performance:"},{"type":"list","items":["Press <strong><code>Octave -</code> and <code>Octave +</code> simultaneously</strong>.","The octave shift immediately resets to <strong>0</strong>."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"launchkey-l-4-1-4","title":"4.1.4: Semitone Transposition Protocol","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"4.1.4: Semitone Transposition Protocol","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"To transpose the keyboard in precise chromatic half-steps (semitones) without shifting hand positions:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">       SEMITONE TRANSPOSITION COMBINATIONS:\n1. TRANSPOSE UP (+1 to +12 Semitones):\n   - Hold [Shift] and press [Octave +]\n   - Each press shifts pitch UP by 1 semitone.\n\n2. TRANSPOSE DOWN (-1 to -12 Semitones):\n   - Hold [Shift] and press [Octave -]\n   - Each press shifts pitch DOWN by 1 semitone.\n\n3. DUAL-BUTTON TRANSPOSE RESET:\n   - Hold [Shift] and press BOTH [Octave -] and [Octave +] simultaneously.\n   - Transpose immediately resets to 0 semitones.</pre>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"launchkey-l-4-1-5","title":"4.1.5: Mathematical MIDI Note Boundary Truncation","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"4.1.5: Mathematical MIDI Note Boundary Truncation","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"The universal MIDI standard specifies a 7-bit note range from <strong>0 to 127</strong> (representing notes <code>C-2</code> to <code>G8</code>)."},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">0                                 60                                127\n[=== C-2 ===] . . . . . . . . [=== C3 ===] . . . . . . . . . . [=== G8 ===]\n◄────────────────────── Standard MIDI Spectrum ───────────────────────────►</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Out-of-Bounds Condition</strong>: If an extreme positive octave shift (+3) is combined with a high positive semitone transposition (+12), physical keys at the upper end of the keybed exceed MIDI note number <strong>127</strong>. Conversely, extreme negative shifts can push low keys below MIDI note <strong>0</strong>.","<strong>Hardware Response</strong>: Keys whose calculated pitch falls outside the 0–127 boundary <strong>transmit zero MIDI data</strong>. No error message is generated; the out-of-range physical keys are simply muted/silent until transposition is brought back within legal MIDI boundaries."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Operational Rules Summary","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<strong>mustCover</strong>: Default C1–C6 range with C3 as Middle C; <code>-3</code> to <code>+3</code> octave shifting; simultaneous dual-button octave reset; <code>±12</code> semitone transposition with Shift; Shift dual-button transpose reset; silent truncation of out-of-range MIDI notes outside 0–127.","<strong>mustNotCover</strong>: Acoustic piano fingering rules; speculative microtonal tunings not in firmware."],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Practical Guided Task & Assessment Checkpoint","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Task</strong>: Transpose the keybed up +7 semitones using <code>Shift + Octave +</code>. Play the lowest and highest keys. Then execute the Shift dual-button shortcut to reset transposition to 0 semitones."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Checkpoint Validation</strong>:"},{"type":"list","items":["OLED display confirms <code>Transpose: +7 st</code>, followed by <code>Transpose: 0 st</code> after reset.","Default pitch C1–C6 restored accurately."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"launchkey-m-4-2-2","code":"4.2","title":"The 61-Key Keybed Performance Characteristics","blurb":"Velocity sensitivity determines how physical key-strike acceleration is translated into MIDI Note-On velocity values (1–127). The Launchkey MK4 61 provides four distinct keybed velocity curve profiles in its internal Settings, accommodating","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"launchkey-l-o-12","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Section 4.2 — Key Velocity Response Curves","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Module Overview","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"Velocity sensitivity determines how physical key-strike acceleration is translated into MIDI Note-On velocity values (1–127). The Launchkey MK4 61 provides four distinct keybed velocity curve profiles in its internal Settings, accommodating diverse playing techniques, synth patches, and dynamic requirements."},{"type":"heading","text":"Learning Objectives","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["Locate and navigate the <code>Vel Curve (Keys)</code> parameter within the hardware Settings menu.","Compare the mathematical dynamic response curves of <strong>Soft</strong>, <strong>Normal</strong>, <strong>Hard</strong>, and <strong>Fixed</strong> profiles.","Configure the <strong>Fixed Velocity</strong> numerical parameter across its 1–127 range (default 120).","Formulate the relationship between the Fixed Velocity parameter and the internal Arpeggiator Accent engine."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"launchkey-l-4-2-1","title":"4.2.1: Navigating to Velocity Curve Settings","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"4.2.1: Navigating to Velocity Curve Settings","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Keybed velocity curves are configured directly on the hardware:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">VELOCITY CURVE SELECTION SEQUENCE:\n1. Press the dedicated [ Settings ] button.\n2. Use [ Pad Bank Up / Down ] to navigate to \"Vel Curve (Keys)\".\n3. Use [ Track &lt; &gt; ], [ Encoder 1 ], or the illuminated pads to select:\n   - Soft\n   - Normal (Default)\n   - Hard\n   - Fixed\n4. Press [ Settings ] to exit and store the active curve.</pre>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"launchkey-l-4-2-2","title":"4.2.2: Comparative Analysis of Velocity Profiles","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"4.2.2: Comparative Analysis of Velocity Profiles","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">127 ┌───────────────────────────/   Legend:\n    │                      . - '    ──────── Soft\n V  │                . - '          - - - -  Normal (Linear)\n E  │          . - '   . '          . . . .  Hard\n L  │    . - '     . '       /\n O  │. '       . '       . '\n C  │      . '       . '\n I  │  . '       . '\n T  │'       . '\n Y  │    . '\n  1 └───────────────────────────\n    0       PHYSICAL KEY STRIKE FORCE      100%</pre>"},{"type":"table","headers":["Velocity Profile","Response Characteristic","Optimal Musical Application"],"rows":[["<strong>Soft</strong>","Exponential curve; higher MIDI velocities achieved with light touch","Fast synth solos, organ playing, players with lighter touch"],["<strong>Normal</strong> (Default)","Balanced linear response across full dynamic range","Expressive acoustic piano, electric pianos, general studio tracking"],["<strong>Hard</strong>","Logarithmic curve; requires significant physical force for high velocities","Aggressive playing styles, preventing unwanted velocity spikes"],["<strong>Fixed</strong>","Dynamic sensitivity disabled; all key strikes output fixed value","Organs, vintage analog lead synths, consistent step entry"]],"caption":null}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"launchkey-l-4-2-3","title":"4.2.3: The Fixed Velocity Parameter & Arp Accent Reference","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"4.2.3: The Fixed Velocity Parameter & Arp Accent Reference","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"When <code>Vel Curve (Keys)</code> is set to <strong>Fixed</strong>:"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Parameter Range</strong>: Configured via Settings -&gt; <code>Fixed Velocity</code> from <strong>1 to 127</strong> (Factory Default = <strong>120</strong>).","<strong>Keybed Output</strong>: Every key depression transmits a <code>Note On</code> event with the exact velocity value programmed in <code>Fixed Velocity</code>, regardless of physical strike velocity.","<strong>Dual Engine Linkage</strong>: The numerical value set in <code>Fixed Velocity</code> is also utilized by the <strong>Arpeggiator Engine</strong> as the baseline velocity target when <code>Arp Velocity</code> is disabled in Settings or when generating rhythmic accents."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Operational Rules Summary","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<strong>mustCover</strong>: Vel Curve (Keys) navigation in Settings; four curve profiles (Soft, Normal, Hard, Fixed); default Normal; Fixed Velocity parameter range 1–127 (default 120); dual linkage with Arp Accent engine.","<strong>mustNotCover</strong>: Speculation regarding undocumented custom mathematical curve formulas."],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Practical Guided Task & Assessment Checkpoint","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Task</strong>: Open Settings, switch <code>Vel Curve (Keys)</code> to <code>Fixed</code>, confirm key output in a DAW or MIDI monitor at velocity 120, and then restore <code>Vel Curve (Keys)</code> to <code>Normal</code>."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Checkpoint Validation</strong>:"},{"type":"list","items":["MIDI monitor records steady velocity 120 under Fixed mode.","Restoring to Normal restores dynamic velocity response from 1 to 127.","Settings menu successfully exited with state preserved."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"launchkey-m-4-3-3","code":"4.3","title":"The 61-Key Keybed Performance Characteristics","blurb":"During live studio recording and stage performance, altering a parameter accidentally while checking its current status introduces unwanted sonic artifacts or ruined takes. The Launchkey MK4 61 provides a non-destructive hardware inspection","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"launchkey-l-o-13","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Section 4.3 — Real-time Value Inspection & Parameter Preview","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Module Overview","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"During live studio recording and stage performance, altering a parameter accidentally while checking its current status introduces unwanted sonic artifacts or ruined takes. The Launchkey MK4 61 provides a non-destructive hardware inspection protocol called <strong>Parameter Preview</strong>, enabled via the <code>Shift</code> modifier."},{"type":"heading","text":"Learning Objectives","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["Formulate the technical mechanism of the non-destructive Parameter Preview protocol.","Execute parameter previews across continuous encoders and linear faders without sending MIDI data.","Identify live performance scenarios where parameter preview prevents accidental parameter jumps.","Complete Assessment Gate C."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"launchkey-l-4-3-1","title":"4.3.1: Non-Destructive Parameter Preview Mechanism","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"4.3.1: Non-Destructive Parameter Preview Mechanism","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"When the <code>Shift</code> button is held down:"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>MIDI Transmission Suppression</strong>: Physical movement of any continuous rotary encoder or linear fader is intercepted by the onboard microcontroller and <strong>suppressed from transmission over USB MIDI and 5-pin DIN</strong>.","<strong>OLED Visual Output</strong>: The OLED display immediately updates with a real-time readout of the parameter's stored numerical value and name (e.g., <code>Cutoff: 64</code> or <code>Volume: -6.0 dB</code>).","<strong>DAW State Protection</strong>: Because no MIDI CC or control surface packets are transmitted, the DAW mixer and virtual instruments remain completely unaltered."],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">       PARAMETER PREVIEW SIGNAL FLOW\n+-----------------------------------------------------------+\n| [Shift Held] + [Turn Encoder 1]                           |\n|       │                                                   |\n|       ├──► Microcontroller generates OLED Overlay:        |\n|       │    \"Filter Cutoff: 74\"                            |\n|       │                                                   |\n|       └──► MIDI Output Buffer: BLOCKED (0 bytes sent)     |\n+-----------------------------------------------------------+</pre>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"launchkey-l-4-3-2","title":"4.3.2: Live Performance & Studio Workflow Utility","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"4.3.2: Live Performance & Studio Workflow Utility","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Parameter Preview is essential in three primary workflows:"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Arpeggiator Inspection</strong>: Checking the current Arp Rate (e.g., verifying whether rate is set to <code>1/16</code> or <code>1/8T</code>) before engaging latch in a live take.","<strong>Scale Mode Verification</strong>: Confirming the active musical Scale Type and Root Note without inadvertently altering the key.","<strong>Mixer Fader Pickup Verification</strong>: Reading the physical fader's stored value before engaging fader movement when operating in <strong>Pickup</strong> fader mode."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Operational Rules Summary","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["<strong>mustCover</strong>: Non-destructive Shift+move preview mechanism; MIDI output suppression; real-world live performance utility.","<strong>mustNotCover</strong>: Speculation regarding preview support on non-continuous binary switches."],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Assessment Gate C (Keybed & Performance Validation)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Objective</strong>: Demonstrate complete operational mastery of the 61-key keybed, octave navigation, transpose offsets, and velocity response."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Self-Assessment Checklist</strong>:"},{"type":"list","items":["[ ] State the default power-on range of the Launchkey MK4 61 (<code>C1–C6</code>, with <code>C3</code> as Middle C).","[ ] Shift the octave to <code>+2</code>, then execute the simultaneous dual-button octave reset (<code>Octave -</code> + <code>Octave +</code>) to restore baseline.","[ ] Shift transposition to <code>-5</code> semitones (<code>Shift + Octave -</code>), then execute the Shift dual-button transpose reset to restore 0 semitones.","[ ] Open Settings, change <code>Vel Curve (Keys)</code> to <code>Hard</code>, test the tactile difference on an active synth patch, and restore the curve to <code>Normal</code>.","[ ] Execute a non-destructive Parameter Preview on Encoder 1 while playing keybed notes simultaneously."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]}]};
